mpics Data Analytics using Azure Databricks &amp; Power BI =F0=9F=8F=85

I recently completed a data analytics project focusing on the Olympics, whe=
re I leveraged Azure Databricks for big data processing and Power BI for dy=
namic visualizations.

Project Overview:
This project aimed to explore the wealth of data generated by the Olympics =
to uncover insights about athletes, countries, and trends across various ga=
mes. Using a combination of Azure Databricks for large-scale data processin=
g and transformation, and Power BI for powerful, interactive dashboards, I =
was able to:

=F0=9F=93=8A Analyze athlete performance across different sports and countr=
ies over multiple Olympic Games.
=F0=9F=8C=8D Identify patterns in medal distribution across continents and =
historical trends.
=E2=8F=B1=EF=B8=8F Visualize year-over-year data to track the evolution of =
sports popularity, athlete demographics, and country performance.
Tools &amp; Technologies:
Azure Databricks: For large-scale data processing, transformation, and adva=
nced analytics with Apache Spark.
Power BI: To create interactive dashboards and visualizations, providing de=
ep insights into Olympics data.
Data Sources: Historical Olympics datasets including athlete, event, and co=
untry performance data.
Key Outcomes:
=F0=9F=93=88 Enhanced understanding of global sporting trends.
=F0=9F=8C=9F Created engaging visualizations to display athlete and country=
 performance, medal distribution, and sports progression.
=F0=9F=94=84 Demonstrated how big data can be transformed into actionable i=
nsights using Azure and Power BI.
